Subject: [PATCH 0/2] platform/x86: hp-wmi: OMEN 16-ap0xxx (8D24) board, and automatic fan mode

Two patches for the HP OMEN 16-ap0xxx with board 8D24.

The first adds the board to the list, with the omen_v1_legacy parameters
its siblings 8D26 and 8E35 already use. That gives it the platform
profile and hwmon fan control.

The second fixes the automatic fan mode on omen_v1_legacy boards. On 8D24,
pwm1_enable=2 leaves the fans stopped for up to two minutes, even under
load. hp-wmi renews the firmware's user-defined fan state and then writes
0 as the setpoint, and the EC obeys that 0 until the state times out.
Reading the EC while the state runs out shows the firmware writing 0xff
as its own automatic setpoint. Writing 0xff instead hands the fans to the
EC's curve within two seconds. The commit message has the details, and
the raw measurements are at:
https://github.com/WinTone01/omen-linux-driver/blob/main/docs/research/ec-handover.md

Only 8D24 has been measured. Testing on an 8D26 or 8E35 would be welcome:
with pwm1_enable=2 under load, the fans should follow the load within
seconds instead of stopping.

